  "articleBody": "Ever wonder why sometimes tiles just don't sit right? A big part of a smooth, even tile floor is all about the prep work underneath. If the surface isn't clean and perfectly level to start, you're setting yourself up for trouble. We're talking about more than just sweeping here; sometimes, the substrate itself needs some TLC. If it’s not structurally sound or if there are existing floor issues, those need to be addressed first. You might need crack isolation, waterproofing, or even vapor control depending on your situation. Also, using the wrong type of adhesive or not applying enough mortar can lead to tiles lifting or having 'hollow spots' where they aren't fully supported. That's why it's so important to have a pro come in and assess the subfloor. They can tell you exactly what kind of prep your specific project needs to make sure your new ceramic tile lasts and looks amazing. Don't skip the foundation!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}